 "summary": "An amber caution: one inertial reference has failed, so one side loses attitude and heading (red ATT flag on the PFD, red HDG flag on the ND). The only ECAM action is on the pedestal switching panel: ATT HDG to CAPT 3 for IR 1, F/O 3 for IR 2, plus the transponder system. If the IR FAULT light flashes, the IR may give attitude again in ATT mode through the QRH IR ALIGNMENT IN ATT MODE procedure.",
