 "background": [
  {
   "text": "Each ADIRS has two parts (ADR and IRS) that may fail independently. The IRS part may fail totally or may be available in ATT mode.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-NAV",
     "page": "P 1/20",
     "pdf": 478
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A single NAV ADR FAULT or NAV IRS FAULT is a simple procedure: only action on the switching panel as indicated by the ECAM.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-NAV",
     "page": "P 1/20",
     "pdf": 478
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "ATT HDG selector: NORM — ADIRU 1 supplies PFD 1/ND 1, ADIRU 2 supplies PFD 2/ND 2. CAPT 3 — IR 3 replaces IR 1. F/O 3 — IR 3 replaces IR 2.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-34-NAV-10-20",
     "page": "P 3/6",
     "pdf": 2102
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If ADIRU 2 fails, the ATT HDG selector has to be set to F/O 3 to maintain side 1 / side 2 segregation; ADIRU 3 is then supplied by GPS receiver 2.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-34-NAV-15-10",
     "page": "P 3/4",
     "pdf": 2122
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "IR FAULT light flashing: attitude and heading may be recovered in ATT mode. Steady: the IR is lost.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-34-NAV-10-20",
     "page": "P 2/6",
     "pdf": 2101
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In ATT mode the IR gives only attitude and heading (heading entered on the MCDU, reset about every 10 min). Once an IR is set from NAV to ATT or OFF in flight, NAV mode is lost for the rest of the flight; it is recovered only on ground by a complete alignment.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-34-NAV-10-20",
     "page": "P 2/6",
     "pdf": 2101
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "technique": [
  {
   "text": "The PF usually remains PF for the entire flight, unless the captain re-allocates tasks or a failure impacts the PF's FLY task.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "AOP-30-30",
     "page": "P 1/6",
     "pdf": 82
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "IR MODE selector actions are crosschecked by both pilots before acting in flight.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "AOP-30-20",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 80
    },
    {
     "book": "PDP",
     "code": "Management of abnormal operations",
     "page": "XFTDN6ECAM00001",
     "pdf": 432
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
